  "scientific_caveats": [
    "MERFISH is a single WT male B6J brain; sampled-cell proportions are not independent animal statistics, absolute tissue cell counts or density.",
    "RNA-seq is RFP-sorted transgenic reporter sampling, not a tissue composition estimate or WT-only atlas.",
    "Even exact-age P58 contrasts retain completely confounded region and library-preparation dates; they are descriptive differences and cannot isolate a regional biological effect.",
    "Independent biological pool identity is unestablished; no cell/section/hemisphere pseudoreplication or animal-level P values are permitted.",
    "Rare non-neuronal strata, including P58 VLMC 3 versus 1 cell, must be interpreted as sparse reporter-selected observations.",
    "Mean differences are natural log1p CP10k-scale differences, not model-derived log2 fold changes.",
    "PBM source effects, baseline atlas differences and adenosine flux/sleep threshold remain separate interpretations; local stimulation ROI requires validated CCF mapping/optical footprint.",
    "SMART-seq matched metadata strata use read CPM and remain separate from 10x UMI measurements; normalization and weight definitions are recorded separately.",
    "SMART-seq shared displayed strata have exact ages P53/P54/P55/P56/P59, with no exact metadata intersection to the primary P58 10x comparison; assay replication is not established.",
    "SMART-seq n >= 10 is a display filter, not evidence of statistical power or animal-level inference."
  ],
